Lets the core show an agent's page live in a view of the app's, as a tile the user watches it work
in (#4115), through content::SetPageTile. A tile's views take no pointer, cursor, tooltip or drop,
never take the keyboard, and don't tell the page the frame or screen the tile moves them to, so the
page keeps its size and screen and the core scales its layer into the tile. Visibility is
untouched: the page draws while the tile is on screen, as one its window shows does. A hook only:
the core decides which pages are tiles.

